package views

templ TermsPage() {
	@legalPage("Terms of service", "2026-10-14", "October 14, 2026") {
		<section>
			<h2>1. About these terms</h2>
			<p>
				afastchat is operated by ByteBridge LLC ("we", "us"). These terms govern your use of
				afastchat.com. Contact us at <a href="mailto:contact@bytebridge.company">contact@bytebridge.company</a>.
				By creating an account or using afastchat, you agree to these terms.
			</p>
			<p>You must be at least 18 and legally able to enter into this agreement.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>2. The service and your account</h2>
			<p>
				afastchat is a chat interface that answers questions using AI models and web search through
				your own OpenRouter account. You are responsible for your OpenRouter account, its charges, and
				keeping your Google account secure.
			</p>
			<p>
				Features and models may change or become unavailable. We do not guarantee uninterrupted
				availability or a particular result. These limitations do not affect any rights you have by law.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>3. Your content and AI output</h2>
			<p>
				You keep your rights in what you submit. You let us store, process and send it to our service
				providers as needed to run afastchat, as explained in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				AI output can be wrong, incomplete or outdated, and cited sources may not support it. Check
				important information before relying on it. Do not use afastchat as a substitute for
				professional medical, legal or financial advice.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
			<p>
				Do not use afastchat to break the law, infringe others' rights, harm or harass people, attack or
				overload the service, or violate the terms of OpenRouter or the model providers you use. We may
				suspend or close accounts that do.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>5. Ending your use</h2>
			<p>
				You can stop using afastchat and delete your account in Settings at any time. We may stop offering
				the service with reasonable notice.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>6. Liability</h2>
			<p>
				afastchat is provided "as is". To the extent permitted by law, we are not liable for indirect or
				consequential losses, or for charges on your OpenRouter account. Nothing in these terms limits
				liability that cannot be limited by law.
			</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>7. Changes</h2>
			<p>
				We may update these terms and will change the date above when we do. Material changes will be
				announced through the service. Continuing to use afastchat after a change means you accept it.
			</p>
		</section>
	}
}
